{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\nA read-only page for GitHub Projects (v2), shown as a board. Boards need the full width, so this is a separate page (slot 7 once #118 folds the Actions page into the GitHub page) rather than a column of the GitHub page. Data comes from `gh project list / view / item-list / field-list --format json`.\n\n`gh project` needs the `project` token scope; when it is missing the page shows a notice suggesting `gh auth refresh -s project` instead of failing.\n\n## Non-goals\n- Read-only, like every vig page: no moving items between columns, no field edits, no item creation / deletion.\n\n## Notes\n- Thanks to the `pages` node, users who do not use Projects can drop it from `pages`.\n- Column order follows the `Status` single-select options as ordered on GitHub; items without a status go into a `No status` column.\n- `gh project item-list --limit` is set high (e.g. 500); when truncated the status bar says `(truncated)`.\n- Demo material: a small project linked to a td72 repository (never a real client project).\n\n## Sub-issues\n- #120 — Projects: page skeleton\n- #121 — Projects: project list pane\n- #122 — Projects: board pane\n- #123 — Projects: item detail pane\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-30T08:11:54Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":119,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Projects view"}
